# Aurora — Environment Variables
#
# Copy this file to ~/.config/opencode/.env and fill in your values.
# The setup.sh script can do this automatically for you.
#
# This file is a template — it contains NO secrets.
# The real .env file must NEVER be committed to the repository.

# ─── Required ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# LLM provider keys: set the env vars expected by YOUR provider configuration.
# scripts/configure-models.sh resolves the role policy against the providers
# you configure and writes the live OpenCode config.
# IMPORTANT: OpenCode does NOT load .env files into its process environment —
# any key referenced via {env:...} in opencode.json must be exported in your
# shell rc instead (see the setup.sh managed block).

# NOTE: IDB_UDID and IDB_PATH (iOS Simulator MCP) are also NOT stored here.
# They are exported in the managed shell rc block, because the ios-simulator
# MCP reads its process environment only (no .env fallback). setup.sh asks for
# them and writes the block automatically.

# ─── MCP servers & integrations ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Memory server local dev DSN (docker compose stack of the private server
# repo — credentials belong to that compose file, never embedded here).
# Used by scripts/setup-memory.sh when DATABASE_URL is not set.
# AURORA_MEMORY_DEV_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://127.0.0.1:5433/aurora

# GitLab token (glab CLI, GitLab-backed MCP integrations)
# Create a Personal Access Token in your GitLab instance:
#   https://<your-gitlab-host>/-/profile/personal_access_tokens
GITLAB_TOKEN=

# Figma token (design-qa contract captures, design system sync tooling)
# Create a Personal Access Token at: https://www.figma.com/settings → Security → Personal access tokens
# Scopes: file_content:read, file_metadata:read, library_content:read (+ file_variables:read if available on your plan)
FIGMA_TOKEN=

# Trello API credentials (task-workflow step 7 bis: post the MR link as a
# comment on the linked Trello card).
# One-shot setup: open https://trello.com/appkey with your Trello session, copy
# the API key, then generate a personal token from the same page.
# NOTE: the token grants full read/write access to your Trello account — same
# exposure class as GITLAB_TOKEN. Never commit the real values.
# Without these credentials the skill falls back to the browser-debug path
# (see skills/task-workflow/SKILL.md, step 7 bis).
TRELLO_API_KEY=
TRELLO_TOKEN=

# ─── Private overlay ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Company/private integrations (custom LLM providers, internal APIs, events
# endpoints) are documented in the private overlay's own env template —
# never in this public repo.
